# Icons

Aesir wraps Lucide and project-specific SVGs behind one component. Import individual icon modules for application code; use a registered `name` when the icon is selected dynamically.

## Basic usage

Pass an imported Lucide component through `icon`. Individual imports let the bundler include only the icons the application uses.

<DocsExample title="Icon usage" source={iconExampleSource} htmlSource={iconExampleHtmlSource}>
	<IconExample />
</DocsExample>

## Size, color, and controls

Icons use `1em` by default and inherit `currentColor`. Set an explicit size for controls or display icons. Icon-only buttons require an accessible label on the button; their icons remain decorative.

<DocsExample title="Icon properties" source={iconPropertiesExampleSource} htmlSource={iconPropertiesExampleHtmlSource}>
	<IconPropertiesExample />
</DocsExample>

## State

Forwarded `class`, `style`, and SVG attributes make state-driven styling possible. Keep the state and accessible name on the control.

<DocsExample title="Stateful icon" source={iconStateExampleSource} htmlSource={iconStateExampleHtmlSource}>
	<IconStateExample />
</DocsExample>

Use `AesirIconSwap` when one action changes between two icons. Both icons stay mounted, so the transition can reverse without replacing the SVG node.

<DocsExample title="Icon swap" source={iconSwapExampleSource} htmlSource={iconSwapExampleHtmlSource}>
	<IconSwapExample />
</DocsExample>

## Composed icons

Nested content renders inside the outer SVG. Keep all geometry inside its view box and add a `label` when the composed icon carries meaning by itself.

<DocsExample title="Composed icons" source={combinedIconExampleSource} htmlSource={combinedIconExampleHtmlSource}>
	<CombinedIconExample />
</DocsExample>

## Custom icons

Project-specific SVG components use the same `AesirIcon` API as Lucide icons.

<DocsExample title="Custom icons" source={customIconsExampleSource} htmlSource={customIconsExampleHtmlSource}>
	<CustomIconsExample />
</DocsExample>

A custom icon component should accept `color`, `size`, and `mirrored`, spread remaining attributes onto its root `<svg>`, and define only its view box and geometry. Render it through `<AesirIcon icon={MyIcon} />`, not directly.

## Guidelines

- Use `16` or `20` pixel icons in text and controls, and `24` for larger UI elements.
- Match icon stroke weight to adjacent text.
- Prefer `currentColor` so icons follow interactive and theme states.
- Animate `transform` and `opacity`, and provide a reduced-motion fallback.
